    {
      "id": "OCR-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-odd-reflection-square",
      "title": "From the reflected index to the square of the minus torsion count",
      "statement": "For E=(1−J)C, the reflected index bound implies |C/ℓC|≤ℓ·|E[ℓ]|². Thus |E[ℓ]|≤B_F^N gives |C/ℓC|≤ℓ·B_F^(2N) at every layer to which the minus bound applies.",
      "hypotheses": "C is a finite abelian group with an involution J, ℓ is odd and the reflection estimate holds. The cyclotomic application uses n≥1 and the separately proved uniform minus bound.",
      "dependencies": [
        "OCR-01"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-odd-square-bound"
      ],
